# Searching

Imagine opening a school website and typing **“calendar”** into the search bar. Instantly, a short list of pages appears even though the site contains hundreds of documents.

<br>

<img src="https://images.code.org/09f3b6ac8f017d7cae84610b797af6ad-image-1767801900953.png" alt="example of a search bar with results" width="400px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0 40px 10px 20px;">

## Try the Search

A search algorithm has to decide what counts as a match. 

**Before clicking each card, predict which pages might show up.**

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr);gap:16px;margin:24px 0;">

  <details style="background:#F5F7F8;border-radius:14px;padding:18px;box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);">
