---

## What is a searching algorithm?

A **searching algorithm** is a rule a program uses to look through data to find items that match a specific value or keyword.

In JavaScript, searching is often used to scan arrays or strings to find matching data, like locating a student name, a message, or a page based on what a user types.

---

## What is a query?

When you use a search feature, you are asking the computer a question, even if it doesn’t feel like one.

<div style="background-color:#B7E0E5;border-radius:10px;padding:15px;margin:20px auto;max-width:85%;box-sizing:border-box;word-wrap:break-word;overflow-wrap:break-word;">
<p style="font-size:14pt;margin-top:12px;line-height:120%;">
🔍 <strong>Query</strong> is the word, phrase, or request you send to a computer to get specific information back from a larger set of data.
</p>
</div>

A query might be:

- A word typed into a search bar  
- A phrase like a student name or page title  
- A value the program is trying to find inside a list  

The searching algorithm uses the query to decide **what counts as a match** and what does not.

---

## Quick Check

Think about the searches above.

<details>
<summary style="cursor:pointer;display:inline-block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:12px 20px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
Why might “sports” fail to find “Athletics Calendar”?
</summary>

<div style="margin-top:14px;background:#F5F7F8;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;">
Because the search may only look for exact word matches. If the page title says “Athletics” but the user searches “sports,” the program may not see them as related unless it is designed to handle synonyms or related terms.
</div>
</details>

<br>

<details>
<summary style="cursor:pointer;display:inline-block;background:#8148B2;color:white;padding:12px 20px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600;border-radius:999px;list-style:none;">
What should students pay attention to when building search?
</summary>

<div style="margin-top:14px;background:#F5F7F8;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;">
Students should pay attention to what data is being searched, what counts as a match, and how small differences in spelling, wording, or capitalization can change the results.
</div>
</details>

---

## Next Up

Let’s take a look at how searching works in JavaScript and what “matching” really means behind the scenes.

